mador County, CA, US"}}, {"id": 3023391, "taxon_id": 64040, "establishment_means": "native", "place": {"id": 50668, "name": "Sagehen Creek Basin", "display_name": "Sagehen Creek Basin, CA, US", "admin_level": null, "ancestor_place_ids": [97394, 1, 14, 281, 50668]}, "list": {"id": 65376, "title": "Flora of Sagehen Creek - Comprehensive Master List"}}], "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Pinus lambertiana</b></i> (commonly known as the <b>sugar pine</b> or <b>sugar cone pine</b>) is the tallest and most massive pine tree, and has the longest cones of any conifer. The species name <i>lambertiana</i> was given by the British botanist David Douglas, who named the tree in honour of the English botanist, Aylmer Bourke Lambert. It is native to the mountains of the Pacific coast of North America, from Oregon through California to Baja California.", "vision": true}}